{
  "id": "8f760a9b-3ce8-4932-8286-67d742397f2e",
  "featureId": "ebb9ceb0-ea12-4374-af6e-12aa4256bcc3",
  "number": 68,
  "shortId": "6ZND9",
  "priority": 12,
  "slug": "context-menu-contextual-menu-overlayhost-plugin-declarable",
  "title": "context-menu: Contextual menu → OverlayHost + plugin-declarable",
  "discussedAt": "",
  "contextReady": false,
  "contextReadyReason": "",
  "summary": "Context menus as a host-owned, context-resolved overlay. Foundation: ContextPath (dotted) + ContextMenuRegistry (built-in providers + plugin Contribution::ContextMenu) + resolve_active_context (keyboard implicit) + unified open_context_menu_for + overlay_origin_mode (mode-restore after close). Keyboard prefix+> works everywhere via prefix arm in SidebarNav; after close the user returns to the origin mode (e.g. stays in sidebar). Mouse right-click refactored to the same unified path (parity preserved, Open-link via target hyperlink). Plugin menus attach by context_path and appear when that context is active/clicked.",
  "description": "Context menus become a host-owned, context-resolved overlay (not hardcoded pane-vs-sidebar branches in the handler). The keyboard-open (`OpenContextMenu` / `prefix+>`) and the mouse right-click both resolve to a `(ContextPath, target)` pair and go through one unified `open_context_menu_for` that looks up registered providers (built-in + plugin `Contribution::ContextMenu`) merged by weight.\n\nArchitecture (locked 2026-07-09):\n- **ContextPath**: dotted string (`pane`, `sidebar.pane`, `sidebar.column`, `sidebar.workspace`, `floating_pane`, future plugin paths). Target is opaque data (pane_id / ws_idx / …) passed to the provider's `build(ctx, target)`.\n- **ContextMenuRegistry**: built-in providers for the 4 paths (migrated from `mouse::open_context_menu` / `open_sidebar_context_menu` item-build) + plugin `Contribution::ContextMenu { context_path, weight: Vec<i64>, build }` (context-menu-5, C1/C2/C3). Lookup collects all matching providers, merges by weight (Dewey), opens one dropdown.\n- **resolve_active_context(state)**: keyboard implicit resolver — `InputMode::SidebarNav`+current item → `sidebar.<kind>`; `Normal`+focused pane → `pane`; future modes plug in.\n- **pending_context**: `Option<(ContextPath, Target, Option<InputMode>)>` — captured in the sidebar prefix arm BEFORE transitioning to Prefix (because `handle_prefix_mode` sets Normal before dispatch, input.rs:277). `handle_open_context_menu` reads `pending_context.take()` as an override of `resolve_active_context`.\n- **open_context_menu_for(state, path, target, anchor, source, origin)**: unified open. Mouse passes `origin=None` (capture current if restorable); keyboard-from-mode passes the explicit origin.\n- **overlay_origin_mode: Option<InputMode>**: restorable mode. On open: capture current if restorable (SidebarNav whitelist) or use explicit origin; don't overwrite if already set (stack). On `resolve()` close (chrome/overlay.rs:362): if no overlay remains AND origin set → `input_mode = origin.take()`. Satisfies: open menu from sidebar → close → stay in sidebar. Modal owns keys while open (events.rs:125), so mode is frozen during.\n- **Prefix arm**: `handle_sidebar_nav_mode` gets `else if ctx.is_prefix` (mirrors `handle_selection_mode`, app/input.rs:738) → `InputMode::Prefix` + arm timeout + capture pending_context. So `prefix+>` resolves via `handle_prefix_mode` → `keymap.resolve(\"normal\", prefix+>)` → `OpenContextMenu`.\n\nMouse consequences: refactored to produce `(path, target)` and call `open_context_menu_for`; parity preserved for built-in menus; \"Open link\" (mouse-only) preserved via `PaneTarget { pane_id, hyperlink: Option<String> }` (keyboard target has `None` → no link entry). Plugin menus appear on right-click once registered (new capability, no regression for built-in).\n\nPlugin contract: declares `context_path` + `weight` + `build(target)`; does NOT pass mode/origin (host-internal). Host includes the plugin menu when the context is active (keyboard) or clicked (mouse).\n\nCode refs: overlay.rs (open_dropdown:253, resolve:360, DropdownSpec:233, DropdownItem), mouse.rs (open_context_menu:115, open_sidebar_context_menu:166, right-click dispatch:441/452), handlers.rs:190 handle_open_context_menu, app/input.rs (handle_sidebar_nav_mode:601, handle_selection_mode:694, handle_prefix_mode:234), app/events.rs:125 (modal owns keys), interaction.rs:265 (OpenContextMenu policy FocusedPaneLocal), actions.rs:299 descriptor.\n\nEdge case (noted): if the menu deletes the selected item (e.g. \"delete workspace\"), the sidebar cursor points to a gone item; the tree rebuilds each frame so the cursor is clamped/reset — no crash, at worst no visible selection.",
  "notes": "",
  "goals": [],
  "nonGoals": [],
  "dependencies": [],
  "dependsOn": [],
  "risks": [],
  "openQuestions": [],
  "decisions": [],
  "acceptedDecisions": [
    {
      "id": "cm-d1",
      "title": "ContextPath dotted + target opaco",
      "decision": "ContextPath è una dotted string (es. \"pane\", \"sidebar.workspace\", \"docker.container\"); target è un dato opaco (pane_id/ws_idx/...). Lookup del registry per path.",
      "rationale": "Plugin-friendly (stringa in config/Contribution), type-safe lato host.",
      "implementationNotes": "ContextPath: String; target: enum/opaque struct passato al provider build(ctx, target).",
      "acceptedAt": "2026-07-09T16:00:00Z"
    },
    {
      "id": "cm-d2",
      "title": "Binding prefix+> ovunque (non tasto diretto in sidebar)",
      "decision": "prefix+> ovunque via prefix arm in handle_sidebar_nav_mode (speculare a handle_selection_mode). Non tasto diretto in sidebar mode (scelta controversa scartata).",
      "rationale": "Stesso binding ovunque, zero sorprese, coerente col pattern selection-mode.",
      "implementationNotes": "else if ctx.is_prefix arm: InputMode::Prefix + arm timeout + cattura pending_context(path,target,origin=SidebarNav).",
      "acceptedAt": "2026-07-09T16:00:00Z"
    },
    {
      "id": "cm-d3",
      "title": "Mode-restore via overlay_origin_mode",
      "decision": "overlay_origin_mode: Option<InputMode> catturato all'apertura (se restorable: SidebarNav whitelist; Normal non catturato → no-op) o via origin esplicito (keyboard da mode). Ripristinato quando l'ULTIMO overlay si chiude in resolve(). Stacked overlay: origin settato una volta, non sovrascritto.",
      "rationale": "L'utente vuole: apri menu dalla sidebar → chiudi → rimani in sidebar. Modal possiede i tasti mentre aperto (events.rs:125), il mode è irrilevante durante; il restore serve solo alla chiusura.",
      "implementationNotes": "Campo su AppState/overlay state; capture in open_context_menu_for; restore in chrome::overlay::resolve() quando layers vuoto.",
      "acceptedAt": "2026-07-09T16:00:00Z"
    },
    {
      "id": "cm-d4",
      "title": "pending_context preserva il target attraverso la dispatch",
      "decision": "Keyboard da sidebar cattura pending_context=(path,target,origin=SidebarNav) nel prefix arm PRIMA di transizionare a Prefix. handle_open_context_menu legge pending_context.take() (override di resolve_active_context); altrimenti resolve_active_context(state) computa da InputMode+focus/selection. Mouse: hit-test produce (path,target) direttamente.",
      "rationale": "handle_prefix_mode setta Normal prima della dispatch (input.rs:277), quindi l'handler non può leggere InputMode::SidebarNav. Segnale esplicito disaccoppia dal mode.",
      "implementationNotes": "pending_context: Option<(ContextPath, Target, Option<InputMode>)> su AppState.",
      "acceptedAt": "2026-07-09T16:00:00Z"
    },
    {
      "id": "cm-d5",
      "title": "Mouse refattorizzato al path unified (parità + Open link via target)",
      "decision": "ContextMenuRegistry: provider built-in registrati per pane/sidebar.pane/sidebar.column/sidebar.workspace (migrazione di open_context_menu + open_sidebar_context_menu item-build). Mouse right-click refattorizzato a produrre (path,target) e chiamare open_context_menu_for. Parità comportamentale per built-in; 'Open link' (mouse-only) preservato via target che porta Option<hyperlink_uri> (keyboard None → niente voce).",
      "rationale": "Unifica mouse+keyboard nel path; nessun regresso visibile per built-in; abilita plugin su right-click.",
      "implementationNotes": "open_context_menu(state,pane_id,pos) e open_sidebar_context_menu(state,item,pos) rimpiazzati da open_context_menu_for. PaneTarget { pane_id, hyperlink: Option<String> }.",
      "acceptedAt": "2026-07-09T16:00:00Z"
    },
    {
      "id": "cm-d6",
      "title": "Plugin: passa context_path+build, non mode/origin",
      "decision": "Il plugin dichiara context_path+weight+build(target); NON passa mode/origin (host-internal). L'host include il menu del plugin quando il context è attivo (keyboard resolve_active_context) o cliccato (mouse hit-test). Costruisce su context-menu-5.",
      "rationale": "Plugin non decide 'quando'; dichiara 'dove'. L'host triggera.",
      "implementationNotes": "Contribution::ContextMenu { context_path, weight: Vec<i64>, build } (C1/C2/C3 già locked in context-menu-5).",
      "acceptedAt": "2026-07-09T16:00:00Z"
    }
  ],
