    {
      "id": "2a269cea-f5a9-421b-9da7-eb1893dc9c00",
      "phaseId": "99d19246-1ba9-4720-9895-e70c66acf144",
      "number": 248,
      "shortId": "SST9A",
      "priority": 9,
      "shortName": "plugin-task-ui-7",
      "title": "plugin-task-ui-7 — Composition-first widgets (every widget accepts a ViewNode)",
      "status": "done",
      "description": "EVERY widget must be able to receive a ViewNode (arbitrary child subtree) as its content — the real SwiftUI/Flutter model.\n\n## Scope (original, locked with user 2026-07-08)\n1. Composition-first widgets [SETTLED done per AGENTS.md]. 2. realize() coverage complete [SETTLED done]. 3. Any ViewNode renders, any widget hosts any widget.\nOverlay direction: base Overlay widget with Modal/Dialog as specializations (composition, not inheritance); BLOCKING STAYS A LAYER PROPERTY; overlay sizing + scrollable body gaps. Update showcase + docs/widgets.md; styling from theme; vocabulary host-owned.\n\n## DONE 2026-07-16 — Part 2 steps 2+3, USER-VERIFIED, commit 431e0d1 (PR #244 to main)\nShowcase page root = ScrollRegion.both() (BUG C fixed); overlays hosted above the scroll in a second tree (BUG B fixed); ScrollRegion children-first wheel + on_layout re-clamp + press-and-hold track paging; Component::overlay_occludes + overlay_occluded_at hook (right-click gate; ToastStack cards / Dialog / CommandPalette / Select impls; ContextMenu deliberately default). Docs + tests complete. User confirmed right-click over page widgets opening the menu is the wanted baseline.\n\n## STEP 4 BUILT 2026-07-16 — base Overlay widget + BUG A fix (uncommitted, AWAITING USER GPU VERIFICATION)\n- NEW heca-grid-ui/src/widgets/overlay.rs: base `Overlay` widget — viewport-filling centering layer, single `panel` child (`.panel()`/`.panel_boxed()` for realized content), BLOCKING AS A LAYER PROPERTY (`.blocking(bool)`: true = scrim + swallow outside input; false = light-dismiss fall-through), `.on_outside_click`, open_signal; focusable/overlay_active while open; overlay_occludes = viewport when blocking else panel rect; standalone event semantics (nested-overlay-first, outside-click hook, blocking swallow). Chrome (scrim/drop-shadow/surface fill/bracket reticle) moved here from Dialog. Anchor-to-rect positioning NOT built yet (no consumer this round) — planned extension.\n- Dialog REFACTORED to compose Overlay: Dialog = full-size passthrough → Overlay (blocking) → panel [title, body?, action-row]. Dialog keeps behaviour (focus trap, field-first keyboard, dismissible policy); paint override deleted (Overlay paints the layer); open signal IS the overlay's.\n- BUG A FIXED at low level, two halves:\n  (a) PAINT: scene.rs overlay segments now carry NESTING DEPTH; Scene::overlay_segments() yields depth-ordered (stable within depth) — a nested overlay (Select list in a Dialog body) composites ABOVE everything its parent draws, including the action buttons painted after it. Tests: nested_overlay_keeps_parent_segment_and_composites_on_top, sibling_overlays_keep_record_order_within_a_depth.\n  (b) INPUT: Dialog offers PointerMoved / Scroll / Widget* intents to an overlay-active descendant FIRST (focus.offer_to_overlay), and presses route through dispatch_trapped when the point is in the panel OR occluded by a nested overlay (overlay_occluded_at) — so an open Select captures hover/wheel/keys over the buttons; Dismiss closes the DROPDOWN (not the dialog), Activate commits its row.\n- Showcase: Dialog body now INCLUDES a nested Select (\"Archive target\") — the deliberately-omitted BUG A case is now the verification demo.\n- heca/src/chrome/overlay.rs test updated to the composed structure (root → Overlay → panel).\n- Docs: widgets.md new §Overlay entry (native + declarative/host-only note), §Dialog rewritten (composes Overlay + nested-overlays-work note), Scene/PaintCx with_overlay table row (depth ordering); AGENTS.md catalogs; overlay-design.md phasing (steps 4–5 built). Full rustdoc.\n- Workspace tests green, clippy clean, showcase builds.\n\nVERIFY (user, GPU showcase): open the Dialog (DELETE PANE button) →\n(a) open the \"Archive target\" Select INSIDE it: its list paints ABOVE the Cancel/Delete buttons (no show-through), buttons under the open list do NOT hover, wheel over the list scrolls the list (not the page), Esc closes the LIST first (second Esc dismisses the dialog), clicking a row commits and closes the list only;\n(b) dialog still centers, scrim still dims, buttons/Input/Checkbox still work, Tab traps, outside click dismisses;\n(c) no regression in the top-level Selects / palette / menu / toasts / page scroll.\n\n## REMAINING after step-4 verification (explicit deferrals, recorded — not silent debt)\n- Overlay anchor-to-rect positioning (clamp + flip) — build when the first specialization converts.\n- Convert Select / Tooltip / ContextMenu / CommandPalette panels to compose Overlay (they keep their own correct placement/chrome today).\n- Fold in overlay sizing (.panel_size) + scrollable body (ScrollRegion in a modal body) gaps from the original scope.\n\n## BUG A — nested Select-in-Dialog (found 2026-07-15) — FIX BUILT (above), awaiting GPU verification. Original diagnosis preserved in docs/overlay-design.md + git history of this task.\n## BUG B — Dialog off-screen in scrolled content — FIXED + verified (431e0d1).\n## BUG C — no horizontal page scroll — FIXED + verified (431e0d1).",
      "notes": "",
